---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
const releases = [
  ['v0.3', 'Visual Planning', 'See the program on a timeline, with planned dependency arrows and bar-edge resizing to adjust scheduled dates without changing effort estimates.'],
  ['v0.4', 'Team & Capacity', 'Check realistic team availability, with guided recurring reservations for meetings and front-office duties per sprint.'],
  ['v0.5', 'Program Calendar', 'Understand work alongside leave, holidays, and program events.'],
  ['v0.6', 'Milestones & Deliveries', 'Track program outcomes and delivery readiness.'],
  ['v0.7', 'Communication', 'Share plans and reports outside the application.'],
  ['v0.8', 'Scenarios & Reconciliation', 'Compare alternatives and reconcile Jira changes.'],
  ['v0.9', 'Stabilisation', 'Improve reliability, usability, and desktop packaging.'],
  ['v1.0', 'Stable', 'Complete the import-to-planning-to-export workflow.'],
];
---

<Page title="Roadmap">
  <h1>Small releases. Useful progress.</h1>
  <p>This is a direction, not a delivery schedule. Planacity is a single-maintainer
    side project; scope stays focused on one useful increment at a time.</p>
  <h2>Current target: v0.2 - Jira Roundtrip</h2>
  <p>Bring Jira work into a local Program Plan and export the agreed structure.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>CSV column and people mapping, validation, and import preview</li>
    <li>Reusable local mapping profiles and preserved imported baselines</li>
    <li>Changes view and configurable Jira CSV export</li>
    <li>Manual planning, local save/open, and JSON backups from v0.1</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="status">The source preview supports the CSV roundtrip workflow. Release review remains;
    no stable release is published yet. Jira APIs and re-import reconciliation are deferred.</p>
  <h2>Later milestones</h2>
  <ul>
    {releases.map(([version, name, goal]) => <li><strong>{version} - {name}:</strong> {goal}</li>)}
  </ul>
</Page>
